<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luanda Island</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ilha de Luanda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda">Luanda</a> Island, or Ilha de Luanda, is a narrow sandy strip, originally an island, off the coast of Luanda, the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>. In the time of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kingdom of Kongo</a> it was a royal fishery where the nzimbu shells used as the kingdom's currency were gathered under the king's control. The Portuguese founded Luanda opposite it in 1576, and it is now a resort and fishing district.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luanda-island.jpg" alt="Luanda Island" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photograph: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luanda_13.23266E_8.80761S.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
